.TH tuer n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuer
.PP
Parses a Mermaid \fBerDiagram\fR (entity\-relationship) block into a \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR model so it renders natively (SVG or PNG) through the pure\-Tcl engine. One of the graph\-type parsers the \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR facade dispatches to; normally call \fBtuflow::toPng\fR / \fBtuflow::toSvg\fR.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tuer 0.2
.CE
.PP
Depends on \fBtclutils::tudiagram 0.3\fR (the crow's\-foot end\-marks).
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tuer::parse text      ;# -> tudiagram model dict
.CE
.SS "Supported syntax (Mermaid subset)"
.CS
ENTITY { type name [key] ... }   -> a box: entity name plus attribute lines
A <cardinality> B : label        -> a connector A--B labelled <label>, with
                                    crow's-foot cardinality marks at both ends
.CE
.PP
Keys (PK / FK) are appended in parentheses on the attribute line. A \fB..\fR (non\-identifying) relationship is drawn dashed, \fB\-\-\fR (identifying) solid.
.SS "Cardinality marks"
.PP
The cardinality on each side of the connector becomes a \fBtudiagram\fR end\-mark (\fB\-startMark\fR on the \fBA\fR end, \fB\-endMark\fR on the \fBB\fR end). The mapping is side\-independent — \fB{\fR/\fB}\fR mean "many", \fBo\fR means "zero (optional)":
.TS
l l l.
Mermaid (left / right)	meaning	end\-mark
\fB||\fR / \fB||\fR	exactly one	\fBexactlyOne\fR
\fB|o\fR / \fBo|\fR	zero or one	\fBzeroOrOne\fR
\fB}|\fR / \fB|{\fR	one or many	\fBoneOrMany\fR
\fB}o\fR / \fBo{\fR	zero or many	\fBzeroOrMany\fR
.TE
.PP
So \fBCUSTOMER ||\-\-o{ ORDER\fR draws "exactly one" at the customer end and "zero or many" at the order end.
.SS Usage
.CS
package require tclutils::tuer
package require tclutils::tudiagram

set src {erDiagram
    CUSTOMER {
        int id PK
        string name
    }
    ORDER {
        int id PK
        int customer_id FK
    }
    CUSTOMER ||--o{ ORDER : places
}
::tclutils::tudiagram::writeSvg [::tclutils::tuer::parse $src] er.svg
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Crow's\-foot cardinality is drawn via \fBtudiagram\fR's \fB\-startMark\fR / \fB\-endMark\fR. v1 limitations (honest): long attribute lists make tall boxes (no scrolling); attribute keys are shown in parentheses rather than a separate column.
.IP \(bu
Companion: \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR (renderer), \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR (dispatch).
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TCLUTILS TUER <REASON>}\fR — \fBEMPTY\fR (no entities found).
